WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:05.472
All right, guys. I need everyone to huddle up and listen.

2
00:00:05.544 --> 00:00:10.200
I'm Coach Bobby, and I'm looking to put together a top-tier team.

3
00:00:10.248 --> 00:00:14.364
Now, I need high-potential pizza athletes who are ready to get in the game.

4
00:00:15.384 --> 00:00:18.984
Now, before we get started, I need each and every one of you to understand

5
00:00:19.008 --> 00:00:19.332
something.

6
00:00:20.544 --> 00:00:24.624
Every shift is a game day, every customer interaction is a play,

7
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.856
and every detail either adds to the customer experience or takes away from it.

8
00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:33.456
Today, we're heading into the film room.

9
00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:37.884
Now, any great athlete knows that if you want to improve your game,

10
00:00:38.543 --> 00:00:43.044
sometimes you got to go back, watch the film, study the details, and

11
00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:47.904
ask yourself one simple question: What did we all do well, and what

12
00:00:47.928 --> 00:00:51.720
can we do better? Because here's the thing about customer service.

13
00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:57.144
Most people think it starts when you smile, say hello, or hand someone a pizza,

14
00:00:57.744 --> 00:00:59.412
but that's only one play in the game.

15
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.440
At Team Wow, customer service starts way before you say a single word.

16
00:01:05.425 --> 00:01:09.480
It's what the customer sees. It's what they hear.

17
00:01:09.504 --> 00:01:14.016
It's how quickly we move. It's the quality of the product we serve.

18
00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:17.400
It's our basic operations behind the scenes.

19
00:01:17.712 --> 00:01:22.332
And ultimately, it's whether or not we deliver on the promise we made to

20
00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:24.084
that customer. So today,

21
00:01:25.464 --> 00:01:29.832
I'm going to be your coach, and we're going to break down some film, the good,

22
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.920
the bad, and the... Well, you guys can figure out the rest.

23
00:01:35.808 --> 00:01:36.577
Let's roll the film.

24
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:45.120
All right, team. First play we're breaking down is store image.

25
00:01:46.056 --> 00:01:50.328
Now, I want you to remember this. The customer starts judging the experience way

26
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.920
before we ever speak to them. Think about it.

27
00:01:53.592 --> 00:01:58.104
Imagine walking into the doctor's office and the floors are filthy, the trash is

28
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.272
overflowing, and there's something mysterious growing in the corner.

29
00:02:02.016 --> 00:02:03.408
Are you staying for that appointment?

30
00:02:04.536 --> 00:02:05.712
No, think not.

31
00:02:06.888 --> 00:02:11.447
Because before the doctor ever says one word, you've already made a judgment about

32
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.736
whether you trust him. Our customers are no different.

33
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.296
They're looking at the parking lot, the windows, the lobby,

34
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.496
counter, floors, and even the restroom.

35
00:02:23.544 --> 00:02:27.816
And yes, even the areas behind the counter that we sometimes convince

36
00:02:27.864 --> 00:02:32.472
ourselves that no one can see. Trust me, they can see it.

37
00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.056
A clean, organized store tells the customer we're prepared, we

38
00:02:37.225 --> 00:02:41.424
take pride in what we do, and that you can trust us with your food.

39
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.368
A dirty, disorganized store sends a completely different message.

40
00:02:46.392 --> 00:02:48.192
And coach isn't going to sugarcoat this one.

41
00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:51.420
A great smile can't save a filthy lobby.

42
00:02:55.176 --> 00:02:59.148
Now, I want you to take a moment and look through the parking lot and look through

43
00:02:59.184 --> 00:03:03.504
the carryout. See how many violations and penalties you can find on the

44
00:03:03.576 --> 00:03:03.984
play.

45
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.880
We definitely dropped the ball on first impressions here.

46
00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:13.800
There are penalties everywhere.

47
00:03:15.096 --> 00:03:17.952
Let's clean this play up and see how it looks.

48
00:03:26.761 --> 00:03:31.128
We definitely dropped the ball on first impressions

49
00:03:31.176 --> 00:03:33.864
here. There are penalties everywhere.

50
00:03:35.184 --> 00:03:38.040
Let's clean this play up and see how it looks.

51
00:03:43.392 --> 00:03:45.816
All right. Now that makes coach a lot happier.

52
00:03:46.608 --> 00:03:51.240
Notice all of the key changes that are very noticeable before we

53
00:03:51.288 --> 00:03:52.800
even talk to an employee.

54
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.388
Take a moment and write in your notes section,

55
00:03:57.408 --> 00:04:02.004
what three ways can we as a team ensure that our stores look like

56
00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.228
this every single day?
